  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday Night through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1134 AM CDT Sat Jul 18 2026\n\nInto the work week, temperatures will only continue to increase as \nWAA increases at 850mb. This will lead to triple digit heat indices \ninto early next week, some getting into Heat advisory territory \nespecially on Tuesday. We will have to evaluate the need for a heat \nproduct as we continue to approach that point in time. Remember to \nstay hydrated and take frequent breaks in the AC or shade if you \nwork outside or have any activities planned. Until the cold front \ncomes through on Wednesday bringing cooler and less humid air into \nMiddle Tennessee, diurnal thunderstorms will continue to be a daily \nthreat. Most of these will not be strong, but we could see some \ngusty winds and localized flash flooding from stronger or training \nstorms due to aforementioned atmospheric setup.\n\nTuesday into Wednesday, a 500mb trough and accompanying low pressure \nsystem will swing through Ontario, dragging behind them the cold \nfront we will see Wednesday. This will bring us some forcing so we \nwill have to watch the convection we get on Tuesday and Wednesday \nuntil FROPA. Not expecting any severe weather at this time, but we \nwill see how the CAMs feel about it once we enter the shorter range \nforecast period. After the cold front, we will enter a quieter \nperiod for the mid-week. Highs will be in the mid 80s starting on \nWednesday, slowly warming back into the 90s into next weekend.",
